WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:04.060
Imagine it's the year 1900.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.350
The horse and buggy still reign
supreme as the choice mode

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.462
of transportation,

00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:10.590
but a relative newcomer,

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.423
the automobile,

00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:13.763
is about to become all the rage.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.643
And so roads begin to pave and things

00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:19.453
like gas stations and
traffic lights appear,

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.030
and voila!

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.247
Everything looks different and
probably smells a lot better,

00:00:25.247 --> 00:00:26.870
too.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.860
The transition from horse
to horsepower ushered

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.569
in a complete infrastructural
change that had ripples

00:00:32.569 --> 00:00:34.720
through every sector imaginable

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.803
and made our modern world possible.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.940
A century later,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.870
are we on the cusp

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.163
of another transformation
that of magnitude?

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.460
Today, the world pretty much
agrees on the basic idea

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.920
that we need to get off
fossil fuels and move

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.416
toward more sustainable
solutions to our modern needs.

00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:03.750
The transportation industry
accounts for something

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.130
like 14% of global
greenhouse gas emissions.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.697
And that's one of the largest contributors

00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:10.333
of pollution in the world.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.340
But going electric is not a simple panacea

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.560
for the world's climate problem.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.270
We need to understand that
electric vehicle is very good

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.130
but the battery is not so green.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.160
The more we consume electric vehicles,

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.360
the more we consume electricity

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.420
and electricity is powered

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.623
by polluted materials
like natural gas or coal.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.310
Just like going from 19th
to 20th century mobility,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.530
the very infrastructure
we built our society

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.300
on may need to change.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.330
And a lot of unresolved issues remain

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.590
before this shift goes into full gear.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.480
For example...

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.210
There aren't enough lithium
ion and cobalt resources

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.270
in the world today.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.910
And the whole industry is
centered on making sure

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.543
that there's no anxiety
associated with the range.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.580
Batteries don't grow on trees.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.959
And for every mile you want to go,

00:01:55.959 --> 00:01:57.430
they become heavier,

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.706
which then drains them faster,

00:01:58.706 --> 00:01:59.938
forcing us to stop

00:01:59.938 --> 00:02:01.152
and charge up again

00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:02.262
and again

00:02:02.262 --> 00:02:03.984
and again,

00:02:03.984 --> 00:02:06.093
which of course takes up energy.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.610
And so we're left with
the ultimate riddle.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.490
How can we move with the ease and freedom

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.716
that internal combustion offers

00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:16.573
while successfully reducing
our overall carbon footprint?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.760
Israeli EV startup ElectReon
is helping crack the code.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.600
We don't need to remove the battery at all

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.670
but we need to reduce
the size of the battery.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.820
And this will create a
green solution to all of us.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.630
We took a step back and
we looked at the shift

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.831
to electric vehicles
in a more holistic way.

00:02:35.831 --> 00:02:36.990
And we said okay,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.280
what makes the most sense?

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.870
How can we create a charging
solution where the vehicle

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.090
battery can be as small
as it can possibly be?

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.855
When you think about battery
capacity and battery density,

00:02:48.855 --> 00:02:52.550
not every vehicle requires a huge battery.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.130
Not every vehicle needs to
travel hundreds of miles.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:56.963
So ultimately,

00:02:56.963 --> 00:02:58.660
the vision is to empower the transition

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.009
to electric vehicles
in the most sustainable

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:02.658
and efficient way possible

00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:04.769
whilst ultimately lowering the cost

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:08.210
of ownership of the
vehicles for the owner.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.975
And the existing solutions based

00:03:09.975 --> 00:03:14.460
on plug-in charging will
not do the shift alone.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.650
So we believe

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.785
that wireless charging is the technology

00:03:17.785 --> 00:03:20.640
that can help to accelerate the adoption

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:21.803
of electric vehicles.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.630
Yes, you heard that right.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.883
Car charging wirelessly.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.070
Wireless charging is a
way to transmit energy

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.209
from one coil

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:36.700
to the other coil without
having hard connection

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.020
between the two.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.450
While we're driving,

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.360
we can charge it

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.000
while we're waiting for passengers

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.290
inside the city.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.160
We can charge it

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.860
while we are loading goods

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.810
at the loading dock.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.643
So it means

00:03:47.643 --> 00:03:49.200
that we can charge the vehicle almost

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.543
any time,

00:03:50.543 --> 00:03:51.810
anywhere.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.690
We don't need to carry
a huge battery with us.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.300
We can reduce the size of the battery

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.500
and we can transmit the
energy almost all day long.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.210
We have the copper
coils that are installed

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.043
under the road,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.570
under the roadway or wherever

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:08.080
it is that we're deploying
that transfer energy

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.220
over the air to a receiver

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.680
that's installed directly

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.250
under the vehicle chassis.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.070
Works on the exact same principle

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.413
as an electronic toothbrush,

00:04:16.413 --> 00:04:17.690
or we're seeing a lot

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.436
of new generation wireless
charging for iPhones.

00:04:20.436 --> 00:04:23.420
There's no actual connection
required between the two.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.800
The energy is via the app.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.830
Wireless charging is actually nothing new.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.870
It's use has been around almost as long

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.320
as the discovery of electricity itself.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.880
The principle is based

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.150
on Nikola Tesla discovery

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.199
more than 100 years ago.

00:04:40.141 --> 00:04:42.307
Nikola Tesla,

00:04:42.307 --> 00:04:44.262
was so ahead of his time

00:04:44.262 --> 00:04:46.070
that his vision for wireless energy

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.420
transformation was
buried by his competitor,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.253
Thomas Edison,

00:04:49.253 --> 00:04:50.974
in favor of a less egalitarian

00:04:50.974 --> 00:04:54.203
and more capitalistic system
of energy transmission.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.833
Today,

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:00.075
he's practically worshiped
by the tech elite

00:05:00.075 --> 00:05:02.499
and the Tesla coil remains the inspiration

00:05:02.499 --> 00:05:04.580
for wireless internet connections

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:05.960
as well as charging solutions

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.033
like ElectReon's.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.940
This charging can occur
even when the car is moving

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.230
and comes with a holistic
power management system

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.713
to maximize the process.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.190
ElectReon's technology is made

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.160
up of four major components.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.940
There's the copper coils directly

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.040
under the road.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.030
There's the receiver unit,

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.586
which accepts the energy

00:05:25.586 --> 00:05:28.059
from the copper coils under the road.

00:05:28.059 --> 00:05:29.916
Then that relationship is managed

00:05:29.916 --> 00:05:32.472
by a management unit at
the side of the road,

00:05:32.472 --> 00:05:35.103
which receives energy
directly from the grid

00:05:35.103 --> 00:05:37.080
and then safely transfers it

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.500
to the copper coils under the road.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.250
These three components are managed

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.630
by cloud software,

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.240
which enables us to remotely

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.813
monitor the entire relationship,

00:05:45.813 --> 00:05:48.870
make sure enough energy
is being transferred,

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:52.270
and ultimately charge
and bill for the energy.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.740
The benefits of wireless
charging are huge.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.030
When we look at the transition

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.880
to electric mobility,

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.830
there are a lot of costs incurred

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.880
on the vehicle side

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.610
and on the infrastructure side.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.870
Installing the technology

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.456
means a vehicle's battery capacity

00:06:05.456 --> 00:06:07.373
can be massively reduced,

00:06:07.373 --> 00:06:11.960
which can be up to 50% of the
cost of the vehicle itself.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.270
The vehicle never needs to stop

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:14.600
to charge again.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.690
You can charge with
different amount of energy

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.860
different vehicles on the same platform,

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.960
which is very unique to wireless charging.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.560
Just as in the transition

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.011
from horses to automobiles,

00:06:27.011 --> 00:06:29.840
public infrastructure
plays a critical role

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.326
in enabling mass adoption,

00:06:31.326 --> 00:06:32.990
but making major changes

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.301
to large complex systems

00:06:34.301 --> 00:06:37.400
while they're in use isn't easy.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.720
There is no standard

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.620
for wireless charging dynamically.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.620
Ultimately,

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.453
in order to be able

00:06:43.453 --> 00:06:44.360
to enter the market

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.627
and offer our technology
at commercial scale,

00:06:46.627 --> 00:06:49.980
we need standardization of the technology.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:50.860
So of course,

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:51.693
we're looking,

00:06:51.693 --> 00:06:52.526
in this case,

00:06:52.526 --> 00:06:55.406
at involvement with the local
government municipality,

00:06:55.406 --> 00:06:57.460
regional transport authority,

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.730
whatever it may be,

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.552
that funds the infrastructure deployment

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:01.810
on the one side

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.643
and then the user,

00:07:02.643 --> 00:07:04.020
the vehicle itself,

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.846
or the owner of the
vehicle will be charged

00:07:05.846 --> 00:07:08.240
for the amount of energy
that's transferred

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.020
to them in the same way that you pay

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.364
for roaming services

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:15.280
or a vehicle today is charged.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.629
When you deal with disruptive technology,

00:07:18.629 --> 00:07:21.151
you need to educate the market.

00:07:21.151 --> 00:07:24.070
You need to deal with standardization,

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:24.982
regulation.

00:07:24.982 --> 00:07:26.630
You need to teach lots

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:27.650
of students

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.390
and bring them to the company.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:31.161
You need to gain new knowledge.

00:07:31.161 --> 00:07:34.093
You need to learn from others' mistakes.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.440
We need the electric companies

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.971
and the grid companies to work together

00:07:39.971 --> 00:07:41.866
to figure out how best to deploy

00:07:41.866 --> 00:07:44.260
this technology in terms

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.660
of the grid requirements at scale.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.120
And that's what all of the pilots

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.740
that we're working on are aimed at.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.163
To figuring out all the
pieces of the puzzle.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.850
Implementing this technology sounds

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:56.730
like quite an ordeal,

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:57.810
but then again,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.010
if there's anything that
is constantly being worked

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:00.980
on already,

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:01.993
it's roads.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.331
We're talking about scraping
off just a small amount

00:08:05.331 --> 00:08:06.770
of the center of the road

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:07.876
to deploy the technology

00:08:07.876 --> 00:08:10.010
and doing it as quickly as possible.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.783
So today we can lay a kilometer

00:08:11.783 --> 00:08:13.095
in just one night.

00:08:13.095 --> 00:08:16.880
So really limiting impacts to the road.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.713
You know,

00:08:17.713 --> 00:08:19.030
if we're doing it on one side of the road,

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.768
then the public can
still use the other side

00:08:20.768 --> 00:08:22.760
of the road the different direction

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.609
and making sure that as much

00:08:23.609 --> 00:08:25.442
of the preparatory work is done

00:08:25.442 --> 00:08:27.070
ahead of time as possible,

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:30.010
limiting impacts to road users.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.310
In a few hours,

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.525
we can take an existing electric vehicle

00:08:33.525 --> 00:08:36.571
and we can install our
unique receiver pad,

00:08:36.571 --> 00:08:38.663
connect it directly to the battery,

00:08:38.663 --> 00:08:40.440
and then you can drive.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.517
So it's very easy to convert

00:08:41.517 --> 00:08:43.386
or to deal with any type,

00:08:43.386 --> 00:08:45.822
any kind of electric vehicles.

00:08:45.822 --> 00:08:47.560
What's really interesting

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.890
about this technology is how it fits

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.580
into each different type or use case.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.363
So of course there are
the vehicles that long,

00:08:55.363 --> 00:08:56.235
long range.

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.068
You know,

00:08:57.068 --> 00:08:58.480
long haul trucking companies,

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.400
for example,

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.740
traveling between states or

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.510
between countries want
an extended mileage.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.100
When we think about last
mile or delivery vans,

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.330
well they're limited today

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.088
by the vehicles battery capacity

00:09:10.088 --> 00:09:12.580
and how often they need to charge.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:13.413
But essentially,

00:09:13.413 --> 00:09:14.246
with this technology,

00:09:14.246 --> 00:09:16.390
they could run double shifts.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:17.872
If we look at city taxes,

00:09:17.872 --> 00:09:19.951
just as an example from the mobility

00:09:19.951 --> 00:09:21.267
as a service world,

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:25.450
they're also limited by the
amount of charge required.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.169
Ultimately, if we installed
charging technology

00:09:28.169 --> 00:09:30.170
along the areas where they were resting,

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.191
they'd be able to
operate for longer hours.

00:09:32.191 --> 00:09:33.723
Buses, too,

00:09:33.723 --> 00:09:36.270
which operate on fixed routes.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.781
So it makes perfect sense for them

00:09:38.781 --> 00:09:39.614
to be able to charge

00:09:39.614 --> 00:09:40.447
while driving and save downtime.

00:09:40.447 --> 00:09:43.410
There is a huge need for electric busses.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.070
So we decided to start with this section.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.100
We have one kilometer of electrified road,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.320
then we will drive the bus,

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.260
and you will see that it transmits energy

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:52.093
during driving.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.120
Every hour,

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.430
we get 75 kilowatts charging the bus.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.572
That means that in two hours,

00:09:58.572 --> 00:10:00.659
we get 150 kilowatts.

00:10:00.659 --> 00:10:02.380
This is half of the amount

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.973
of energy that the bus
needs to drive all day long.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.700
That means that we can reduce the size

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.340
of the battery by half

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.120
and lead to great savings
and cost of the bus battery

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.143
and the bus itself.

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:15.841
Once we're going to drive the bus,

00:10:15.841 --> 00:10:16.674
we're going to see

00:10:16.674 --> 00:10:18.740
that the bus driver doesn't
need to do anything.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.030
This is the beauty of it.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:20.863
For him,

00:10:20.863 --> 00:10:21.696
it's a normal bus.

00:10:21.696 --> 00:10:24.179
He doesn't need to change
anything in his driving.

00:10:24.179 --> 00:10:27.080
ElectReon is not relying
on this test site alone.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.080
As a proof of concept,

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.230
they have several
projects around the globe

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.780
in various stages.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:35.256
We have a project in Gotland, Sweden

00:10:35.256 --> 00:10:38.610
where we show the
charging of a large truck,

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:39.480
a 40 ton truck,

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:43.650
and a large electric
bus showing the capacity

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:44.780
for battery reduction.

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:46.450
As the vehicles are charged directly

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.373
from the road in Tel Aviv,

00:10:48.373 --> 00:10:50.760
we're showing that ultimately,

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.607
a bus can operate an extended

00:10:52.607 --> 00:10:56.420
or 24 seven service with
higher frequency trips

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.050
because it doesn't need to stop
for dedicated charging time.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:00.883
In Italy,

00:11:00.883 --> 00:11:03.168
we're going to be deploying
an interesting project

00:11:03.168 --> 00:11:05.560
with a toll road operator,

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.310
which is a classic use case for us,

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.143
right?

00:11:08.143 --> 00:11:08.976
If you,

00:11:08.976 --> 00:11:09.809
as a user,

00:11:09.809 --> 00:11:10.642
are already paying to use a toll road,

00:11:10.642 --> 00:11:13.320
why not also get energy
transfer to your vehicle

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.083
then and charge your car?

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.500
Part of ElectReon's vision is in alignment

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.169
with the trend of increasing public spaces

00:11:21.169 --> 00:11:23.732
in urban environments.

00:11:23.732 --> 00:11:25.970
We're talking about infrastructure

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.340
that's essentially invisible.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:28.173
It's under the road,

00:11:28.173 --> 00:11:29.950
so no changes to the road surface,

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.176
no noise,

00:11:31.176 --> 00:11:34.590
no additional use of space.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.001
So if we look at the urban environment,

00:11:36.001 --> 00:11:36.834
for example,

00:11:36.834 --> 00:11:39.187
it makes more sense to
have dedicated space

00:11:39.187 --> 00:11:40.489
for pedestrians,

00:11:40.489 --> 00:11:42.400
for cyclists,

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.193
to increase the amount of space for them

00:11:44.193 --> 00:11:45.840
and to not have the focus

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.083
on the visible charging infrastructure.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:53.022
In keeping with Nikola
Tesla's egalitarian ideals,

00:11:53.022 --> 00:11:55.389
ElectReon plans on sharing their solutions

00:11:55.389 --> 00:11:57.880
with the world at large.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:00.420
So our approach is a bit different.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.320
We are going to offer the IPs

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.577
for free for a car manufacturer

00:12:05.577 --> 00:12:07.840
in order to increase the adoption

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:08.923
of wireless charging.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.000
This sort of open source
IP sharing is typical

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.700
of the Silicon Valley set.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.540
Elon Musk did the same in the hopes

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.550
of moving to a new generation
of sustainable development.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:22.261
As the rising tide does raise all ships.

00:12:22.261 --> 00:12:23.171
ElectReon,

00:12:23.171 --> 00:12:25.260
even as it proves its concept

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.900
and takes on more partners,

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.273
remains in its infancy.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.143
There's still some questions

00:12:30.143 --> 00:12:32.730
about the economics behind their product,

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.270
and if it's able to be deployed

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.103
around the world,

00:12:35.103 --> 00:12:36.160
but they are picking up steam

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.790
with several projects in Europe

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.408
and plans to expand in the U.S.

00:12:40.408 --> 00:12:43.591
and capture on President
Biden's initiative to try

00:12:43.591 --> 00:12:46.883
to ramp up EV infrastructure
in the country.

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:50.770
That's a big if since there's no guarantee

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.343
that ElectReon will receive the benefits

00:12:52.343 --> 00:12:54.300
of Biden's infrastructure plan,

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.020
not to mention that
they're not the only game

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:56.940
in town.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.162
Siemens eHighway,

00:12:58.162 --> 00:12:59.160
Elways,

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.385
and ELONROAD

00:13:00.385 --> 00:13:04.010
all claim to have commercial-ready
electric road systems,

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.730
but the ElectReon team and their
ambitions remain undeterred

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.220
by competition and held strong

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.470
by an unwavering faith
in their core mission.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.210
The real question is,

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.520
is what are we doing to limit
the environmental impacts

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.511
of electric mobility?

00:13:19.511 --> 00:13:21.600
How are we making it truly sustainable?

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.710
And that's how I was really able to get

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.250
behind the vision that
the founders have here

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.750
and what they're trying to do.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:31.497
And as for the daunting task
of altering the world's roads

00:13:31.497 --> 00:13:33.159
for wireless charging,

00:13:33.159 --> 00:13:36.880
ElectReon is taking it
one kilometer at a time.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.040
When you start something
that at the beginning

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.240
you need to put lots of effort

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.231
to start moving this change.

00:13:42.231 --> 00:13:44.318
But once you are in motion,

00:13:44.318 --> 00:13:46.790
then it will be much easier to move fast

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.264
and fast and accelerate.

